# An extension's side panel asks which tab the user is looking at, as ChatGPT's panel does
# before it reads the page: chrome.tabs.query({active: true, lastFocusedWindow: true}). In Chrome
# that is the page beside the panel. In Cra the panel page sits in a Chromium window of its own,
# so the query gave the panel itself, and ChatGPT refused to read a chrome-extension:// page.
budget rss=700 stalls50=5
from://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/SidePanelExtension
relaunch
from://open?url=${PAGE}?n=active
wait 3
from://debug?extensionAction=${SIDE_PANEL_EXTENSION_ID}
expect-log side panel shows ${SIDE_PANEL_EXTENSION_ID} in Default
wait 2
from://debug?windowSize=1400x880
wait 1
from://debug?clickAt=1300,400
wait 1
from://debug?sidePanelJS=probeTabs()
wait 1
from://debug?sidePanelJS=tabsSeen
expect-log side panel evaluates tabsSeen to last-page-current-page-listed-none-window-page$
from://debug?removeExtension=${SIDE_PANEL_EXTENSION_ID}
wait 1
reject-log fault:
